# All variables here are Vite build-time env vars (VITE_* prefix) and end up
# readable in the shipped client bundle — this file must NEVER contain
# secrets. There was no .env.example in this project before; it's added here
# purely to document the 3 vars the code actually reads (see
# src/integrations/supabase/client.ts and src/lib/auth-redirect.ts).
#
# None of these are required to run the app — every one has a working
# fallback baked into the code already (the public Supabase project URL +
# anon key, and window.location.origin for the site URL). Only set them if
# you specifically need to override a fallback (e.g. pointing a local
# checkout at a different Supabase project).
#
# Gmail SMTP / Resend credentials do NOT go in this file, or in any .env
# file, ever. SMTP for Supabase Auth's own emails (signup confirmation,
# password reset) is configured entirely in the Supabase Dashboard under
# Authentication → Settings → SMTP Settings. The separate Resend-based
# in-app emails (new-device sign-in alerts, email-linking OTP) read their
# key from a Supabase Edge Function secret (`Resend_api_key`, `EMAIL_FROM`),
# also dashboard-only — never a VITE_* var, never this file.

# Public Supabase project URL and anon/publishable key (safe to expose
# client-side by design — this is the anon-role key Row Level Security is
# built to be public alongside, not the service-role secret).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Only needed to override the production-origin fallback used when
# window.location.origin is unavailable or looks like a local/dev origin.
# On an actual deployment (Vercel, Lovable preview, etc.) this is never
# needed — window.location.origin already resolves correctly on its own.
VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
